# Local GitHub Actions runner config (`act`).
#
# Usage:  act workflow_dispatch -j backend-fast
#
# One prerequisite lives in your USER config, not here: `-s GITHUB_TOKEN=`
# in `~/.actrc`. `act` reuses a GitHub token from the environment or the
# `gh` keyring, and a stale or invalid one makes its go-git action fetch
# fail with "authentication required: Invalid username or token" — every
# action clone (`actions/checkout`, `crystal-lang/install-crystal`, ...)
# then dies. An empty token forces anonymous clone, which works for the
# public actions this repository uses. A project `.actrc` may not set
# secrets, so the line must sit in `~/.actrc`:
#
#   printf '%s\n' '-s GITHUB_TOKEN=' >> ~/.actrc
#
# Ubuntu image: `catthehacker/ubuntu:act-latest` carries the tools the
# jobs need. Pull it once with:
#   docker pull catthehacker/ubuntu:act-latest

-P ubuntu-latest=catthehacker/ubuntu:act-latest
